{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can install React Query via "},{"type":"link","href":"https://npmjs.com","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NPM"}]},{"type":"text","value":",\nor a good ol' "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script>"},{"type":"text","value":" via\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://unpkg.com","children":[{"type":"text","value":"unpkg.com"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"npm","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NPM"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm i @tanstack/react-query@4","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/react-query@4","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"yarn add @tanstack/react-query@4","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Query is compatible with React v16.8+ and works with ReactDOM and React Native."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the "},{"type":"link","href":"/query/v4/docs/framework/react/examples/simple","children":[{"type":"text","value":"simple"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"/query/v4/docs/framework/react/examples/basic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"basic"}]},{"type":"text","value":" examples!"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"cdn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CDN"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you're not using a module bundler or package manager we also have a global (\"UMD\") build hosted on the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://unpkg.com","children":[{"type":"text","value":"unpkg.com"}]},{"type":"text","value":" CDN. Simply add the following "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script>"},{"type":"text","value":" tag to the bottom of your HTML file:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script src=\"https://unpkg.com/@tanstack/react-query@4/build/umd/index.production.js\"></script>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once you've added this you will have access to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"window.ReactQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" object and its exports."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This installation/usage requires the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://reactjs.org/docs/cdn-links.html","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React CDN script bundles"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to be on the page as well."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"requirements","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requirements"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Query is optimized for modern browsers. It is compatible with the following browsers config"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Chrome >= 73\nFirefox >= 78\nEdge >= 79\nSafari >= 12.1\niOS >= 12.2\nOpera >= 53"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Depending on your environment, you might need to add polyfills. If you want to support older browsers, you need to transpile the library from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules"},{"type":"text","value":" yourselves."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"recommendations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recommendations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is recommended to also use our "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../eslint/eslint-plugin-query","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ESLint Plugin Query"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to help you catch bugs and inconsistencies while you code. You can install it via:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npm i -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query@4","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query@4","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"or"}]},{"type":"code","value":"yarn add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query@4","lang":"bash"}],"headings":[{"id":"npm","text":"NPM","level":3},{"id":"cdn","text":"CDN","level":3},{"id":"requirements","text":"Requirements","level":3},{"id":"recommendations","text":"Recommendations","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou can install React Query via [NPM](https://npmjs.com),\nor a good ol' `<script>` via\n[unpkg.com](https://unpkg.com).\n\n### NPM\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/react-query@4\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/react-query@4\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add @tanstack/react-query@4\n```\n\nReact Query is compatible with React v16.8+ and works with ReactDOM and React Native.\n\n> Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the [simple](/query/v4/docs/framework/react/examples/simple) or [basic](/query/v4/docs/framework/react/examples/basic) examples!\n\n### CDN\n\nIf you're not using a module bundler or package manager we also have a global (\"UMD\") build hosted on the [unpkg.com](https://unpkg.com) CDN. Simply add the following `<script>` tag to the bottom of your HTML file:\n\n```html\n<script src=\"https://unpkg.com/@tanstack/react-query@4/build/umd/index.production.js\"></script>\n```\n\nOnce you've added this you will have access to the `window.ReactQuery` object and its exports.\n\n> This installation/usage requires the [React CDN script bundles](https://reactjs.org/docs/cdn-links.html) to be on the page as well.\n\n### Requirements\n\nReact Query is optimized for modern browsers. It is compatible with the following browsers config\n\n```\nChrome >= 73\nFirefox >= 78\nEdge >= 79\nSafari >= 12.1\niOS >= 12.2\nOpera >= 53\n```\n\n> Depending on your environment, you might need to add polyfills. If you want to support older browsers, you need to transpile the library from `node_modules` yourselves.\n\n### Recommendations\n\nIt is recommended to also use our [ESLint Plugin Query](../../../eslint/eslint-plugin-query) to help you catch bugs and inconsistencies while you code. You can install it via:\n\n```bash\nnpm i -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query@4\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query@4\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query@4\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: installation\ntitle: Installation\n---\n\nYou can install React Query via [NPM](https://npmjs.com),\nor a good ol' `<script>` via\n[unpkg.com](https://unpkg.com).\n\n### NPM\n\n```bash\nnpm i @tanstack/react-query@4\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/react-query@4\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add @tanstack/react-query@4\n```\n\nReact Query is compatible with React v16.8+ and works with ReactDOM and React Native.\n\n> Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the [simple](/query/v4/docs/framework/react/examples/simple) or [basic](/query/v4/docs/framework/react/examples/basic) examples!\n\n### CDN\n\nIf you're not using a module bundler or package manager we also have a global (\"UMD\") build hosted on the [unpkg.com](https://unpkg.com) CDN. Simply add the following `<script>` tag to the bottom of your HTML file:\n\n```html\n<script src=\"https://unpkg.com/@tanstack/react-query@4/build/umd/index.production.js\"></script>\n```\n\nOnce you've added this you will have access to the `window.ReactQuery` object and its exports.\n\n> This installation/usage requires the [React CDN script bundles](https://reactjs.org/docs/cdn-links.html) to be on the page as well.\n\n### Requirements\n\nReact Query is optimized for modern browsers. It is compatible with the following browsers config\n\n```\nChrome >= 73\nFirefox >= 78\nEdge >= 79\nSafari >= 12.1\niOS >= 12.2\nOpera >= 53\n```\n\n> Depending on your environment, you might need to add polyfills. If you want to support older browsers, you need to transpile the library from `node_modules` yourselves.\n\n### Recommendations\n\nIt is recommended to also use our [ESLint Plugin Query](../../../eslint/eslint-plugin-query) to help you catch bugs and inconsistencies while you code. You can install it via:\n\n```bash\nnpm i -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query@4\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\npnpm add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query@4\n```\n\nor\n\n```bash\nyarn add -D @tanstack/eslint-plugin-query@4\n```\n"}
